<title>BELGIUM: EU rice experts may fix U.S. quota arrangements.</title>
<headline>EU rice experts may fix U.S. quota arrangements.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union's rice management committee may decide on Thursday details of export certificates that are needed to import U.S. rice under GATT quota arrangements, an EU official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;The technical arrangments of the GATT (General Agreement on Tariffs and Trade) world arrangement were not previously fixed because the U.S. had not sorted out their own administrative arrangements,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>The question will be discussed by experts and if agreement is reached will be voted by the EU committee, the official said.</p>
<p>The quota arrangement will allow the U.S. to export to the EU 38,721 tonnes of milled and semi milled rice, 7,642 tonnes of husked rice and 5,461 tonnes of broken rice.</p>
<p>If adopted, the quota will be open for bids five days after the regulation comes into force, which will be three days after it is published in the EU Official Journal.</p>
</text>
